    "name": "APA HOTEL YODOYABASHIEKIMAE",
    "detail": "Japan isn't cheap and from what i gather this is wanna of the standard hotels and a relatively cheap price. The room is tiny, with hardly any space to move around, let alone stow a big suitcase. The bed was a bit on the hard side too (the one in Tokyo is comfier my bf said)! Staff are super friendly and helpful. You're close enough to the metro system in the middle of the business district. We were there during the New Year holiday so it was really quiet in the streets. (Not the best time to visit Japan by the way, as most places are closed or whatever you want to do seems much more difficult than normally). If you are looking for the basics this is a good hotel. ",
